.SH NAME
cbor::edn_literal \- Holds the CBOR bytes of one item that the literal \fR"\&.\&.\&."_edn\fP read from its EDN text at compile time\&.  

.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.PP
\fR#include <cbor/diagnostic_notation\&.hpp>\fP
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP 

.SS "template<std::size_t N>
.br
class cbor::edn_literal< N >"Holds the CBOR bytes of one item that the literal \fR"\&.\&.\&."_edn\fP read from its EDN text at compile time\&. 

Only the literal makes one, so the bytes are always one well-formed item, as \fBcbor::diag2cbor()\fP writes it\&. \fBcbor::lazy::at()\fP takes it as a key or an index\&.

.PP
